message: "If you cite these essays, please cite them using the metadata below."
type: dataset
title: "SISO Foundation: SISO Ontology and SISO Ontology to Computation"
authors:
  - family-names: Bailey
    given-names: Jonathan
abstract: >-
  Two foundational essays of SISO (Stream In, Stream Out). SISO Ontology argues
  that reality is process rather than objects, with thirty-nine annotations
  placing ideas from the process and object traditions. SISO Ontology to
  Computation traces software, devices and ideas from clay tokens to the
  transformer, and what each contributes and where each diverges.
keywords:
  - SISO
  - ontology
  - process philosophy
  - history of computing
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
